[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/Seyche Temple + Beach.png" fade="0.0"]
audio music "res://assets/audio/music/seyche_theme.ogg"
set {ermir_name} = "???"
join "Civillian 2" left [animation="Bounce In" length="0.0"]
join "Civillian 1" right [animation="Bounce In" length="0.0"]
Within a small seaside temple dedicated to Seyche, merchants gather to pray.
Seyche listens to their prayers from a distance until they finish and leave the temple.
"Civillian 1": Oh Great Seyche, please bless our travels. The winds of commerce are approaching, and we pray for your protection in your waters.
leave "Civillian 2"
leave "Civillian 1"
[wait time="3.0"]
audio music -
do ErmirLoop.play_bgm()
join Seyche center
Ermir: Well, well, well![pause=0.6] What oh what! do we have here?
update Seyche left [move_time="1.0"]
join Ermir (Bored) right [animation="Slide In Up" length="1.0"]
Seyche turns around as a heavy gust of wind blows towards her, and sees a winged man flying above her waters.
Ermir: A newborn god that wishes to take over [lspeed=0.01]MY[lspeed] domain and steal [lspeed=0.01]MY[lspeed] prayers that should have been meant for [lspeed=0.01]ME?
Seyche (Uncomfortable): I’m sorry, but who are you…?
Ermir (Laugh): I’m glad you asked!
Ermir (Neutral): Although, you should have known me by now but I will re-introduce myself regardless!
Ermir (Smug): I am the illustrious, [pause=0.5]magnificent, [pause=0.5]amazing, [pause=0.5]and extraordinary god of the winds,
set {ermir_name} = "Ermir"
Ermir (Laugh): ERMIR!
Seyche: Oh… [pause=0.4]another god…?[pause=0.4] It’s ummm… [pause=0.8]nice to meet you?[pause=0.4] I am Seyche, the new goddess of Krishark Sea.
Ermir (Bored): I know that, every god does.[pause=0.4] I came here because of the [lspeed=0.01]AUDACITY[lspeed] of these merchants to pray to.
Ermir: you...
Ermir: -instead of [lspeed=0.01]ME![lspeed] for safe travels.
Seyche (Sad): But…[pause=0.4] they prayed to me for safe travels in my waters, how does that relate to the winds?
Ermir: Ah, [pause=0.4]Of course,[pause=0.4] a young goddess such as yourself wouldn’t understand..
Ermir: Ahem. [pause=0.88]You see, I am not JUST the god of the winds, but the god of travel and merchants as well! Which is why your merchants should have been praying to me instead for safe travels.
Seyche: Ah, [pause=0.8]I’m sorry,[pause=0.5] I didn’t know. [pause=1]But the merchants have already departed and they have already requested my help.
Ermir (Smug): Hah! That leaves one way to settle this…[pause=0.8] a contest!
Seyche (Surprised): A… [pause=0.6]contest?[pause=0.4] What are we supposed to contest for?
Ermir: A storm is coming soon, and those merchant vessels won’t survive all by themselves! [pause=0.4]Why don’t we compete to see who can guide the merchant vessels the best?
Seyche: If so, why don’t we just work together so that the merchants can get through the storm?
Ermir (Neutral): ...
Ermir (Laugh): Snrk- [pause=0.8]HAHAHAH!
Ermir (Bored): You make a good point, [pause=0.2]that would give those merchants better odds of survival.
Seyche (Normal): So you agree that we should work together then?
Ermir (Smug): Well…[pause=0.4] That’s not really a contest now is it?[pause=0.4] Oh wow look at the time the contest has just begun, Goodluck!
Seyche (Surprised): Huh!?
# guide a ship minigame